title: It is drawn only where the subscribee is drawn.
pid: 188500c2-ede2-49a0-a2f8-1a30c6b0b05e
body: |2-
  An occurrence drawn editable (a view's root, among others) gets a
  subscribeeFolder when it subscribes to anything. In it each subscribee
  shows its unintegrated children, and its contains herald reads 'C2/8'
  (two of eight unintegrated). The count belongs to that occurrence
  under that subscriber. The subscriber's own headline says only 'S1':
  nothing on it says that something is new. Under another's fork, Ed
  saw the count 'C1/33' and none of the 33, so no way to tell which.
